  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FOREST OF VERACRUZ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project has been developed according to the priorities and strategies established in the Partners In Flight Business Plan for the Gulf-Caribbean Slope of Mexico and Central America Eastern Deciduous Forest. It will build on previous phases which have protected 3,706 acres of important migratory bird stopover habitats in the Central Coast of Veracruz. This project will increase the amount of protected habitat protected by approximately 12,000 acres, and contribute data that help to determine population trends at a continental level. It will also provide formal training for biologists, and increase an environmental education program to schools and communities in the region. Benefitted species include swallow-tailed kite, Swainson&apos;s hawk, wood thrush, prothonotary warbler, Swainsons warbler, yellow- throated warbler, Kentucky warbler, painted bunting and indigo bunting.</narrative>
  </description>
